      "content": [
        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Finding\n\n**The available evidence identifies an event created 75 minutes after September entered Pending Close. Its recorded `POSTED` status is inconsistent with Oracle’s documented treatment for newly created transactions of this type.**\n\n| Item | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Manufacturing order | **MO-25-09-1070** |\n| Work order ID | **WO-2025-09-004** — Cooler Plate Pack, Racine |\n| Source transaction | **TXN-ISSUE-250930-1070** |\n| Cost event | **CE-250904-0004**, `INPUT` — component issue |\n| Amount | **USD 284,763.42** (**28,476,342 cents**) |\n| Event-created time | **2025-09-30T19:15:00** |\n| September Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** |\n| Time after Pending Close | **75 minutes** — 4,500 seconds |\n| Recorded accounting status | **POSTED** |\n\nThe timestamps above are reproduced exactly as recorded; the source does not specify a time zone.\n\n## Oracle policy assessment\n\nOracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B, **“Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting”** (PDF page 233; printed page 225), states that transactions created after Pending Close—even for the current or a prior period—will not be staged or processed until the period is closed or reopened. Transactions entered before Pending Close can continue processing.\n\nThe documented exceptions are **revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments**. This event is an **INPUT/component issue**, not one of those exceptions. Accordingly, its recorded **`POSTED` status is not consistent with the supplied Pending Close policy**.\n\n## Evidence limitation and delivery\n\nI directly verified the work order, period timestamp, and Oracle policy. The supporting event source was not staged, so the event details above rely on **two corroborating shared audit artifacts from the same source snapshot**, backed by actual source-read receipts, rather than my own direct read of the event row.\n\nNo database records were changed. The audit and provenance were saved to `/cache/work/worker_92896a64ff50/audit-report.json`. The report was submitted, but service validation remains **`needs_evidence`**.",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
      "phase": "final_answer"
    }
  ],
